# The walked twin of unit_held_call_free_name_converted: every method walked.
# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# HELD-FREE-NAME-OTHER-TYPE. A caller's value of another numeric type for a
# held definition's free name is a present candidate: the call that hands
# it converts it to the definition's type by the ordinary conversion, never
# passing it over for the copied value. h0's n is an int, 6; h3's n is a
# size_t, 1000. go calls both. From the root, with no n: 7, and 1001. outer
# has an int n, 40: h0 reads 40, and h3 reads it as 40U: 41 + 100. Entry 7.
fn: make0 (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: f0 () int
        return: n + 1
    return: f0

fn: make3 (size_t: n) fn: () size_t
    fn: f3 () size_t
        return: n + 1U
    return: f3

@: h0 make0(6)
@: h3 make3(1000U)

fn: go () size_t
    int: a h0()
    size_t: b h3()
    if: a > 10
        return: b + 100U
    return: b
end: go

fn: outer () size_t
    int: n 40
    return: go()
end: outer

size_t: x go()
size_t: y outer()
int: ok 7
if: x != 1001U || y != 141U
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
